<!--
  The Kaaba's band and door, drawn on top of ic_kaaba.xml in the dial's face colour so the
  mark reads as a draped cube rather than a plain block. The two viewports are identical
  and both are drawn into the same square, so the coordinates here are in the same frame
  as the silhouette's and must move with it.

  Face colour, not gold. Gold would be truer to the kiswah, and it was rejected: the dial
  face is surfaceVariant normally and primaryContainer the moment you are facing the
  Qibla, and each of those differs again between light and dark, so a gold band would be
  four more colour pairs to hold above WCAG AA — and gold against the silhouette's own
  colour is the weakest of the four in both themes. Painting the detail in the face colour
  means the only pair that has to hold is the one already under test in ColorContrastTest,
  and the band's contrast is then the same as the mark's own by construction.

  The band sits at y 7.5, about a quarter of the way down the wall, which is roughly where
  the hizam sits on the building. It is 1.2 units thick and no thicker: at 2 units the top
  of the cube stopped reading as part of the cube and started reading as a separate lintel
  sitting above it, which made the whole mark look like a shopfront.

  The door is off-centre to the right and stops 1.5 units above the plinth rather than
  meeting it. That gap is doing real work — the door of the Kaaba is raised about two
  metres off the ground, and it is most of what separates this silhouette from a plain box
  with a stripe across it.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FF000000"
        android:pathData="M4.5,7.5h15v1.2h-15z M12.5,11.5h4.5v7h-4.5z" />
</vector>
